From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 11:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] HFR VRR: the sink's fast 1080p as the base, whatever its rate

HFR VRR ran on 1080p165 only where the sink listed that exact mode, and
on 1080p120 otherwise. The kernel now lists the sink's fastest 1080p
above 120 Hz under its own rate ("1920x1080p144hzV", "...240hzV"), read
from its EDID, so a 144 Hz TV or a 240 Hz monitor has one too.

The base is that mode, where the sink's VRR range reaches its rate. It is
told by its timing in the connector's mode list (progressive 1920x1080
faster than 120 Hz, DRM's own refresh rate), not by the text of its name,
and the rate is kept with the base when it is chosen. Everything that
knew the 165 name (the 3D left behind by a Kodi that died, the desktop
it goes back to, the mode that failed and is not tried again) asks
whether a mode is a 3D base.
The film still plays at the largest even multiple of its rate within
120 Hz (95.904 Hz for 23.976 fps): a faster base only draws each eye in
less of its frame.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
