  * What a film rate makes of HFR VRR on the current base mode. A 1000/1001 film
  * rate takes the 119.88 Hz twin of 1080p120, so VRR lands on it exactly; on
- * 1080p165 there is no twin and VRR is told the 1000/1001 rate itself.
+ * a fast 1080p (144, 165, 240 Hz) there is no twin and VRR is told the
+ * 1000/1001 rate itself.
  * vrr_rate is the largest even multiple of the film rate the base carries. On
  * 1080p120 it is in the base mode's nominal units (the driver scales the base
- * line rate by it), so on the twin 9600 is 95.904 Hz; on 1080p165 it is the
+ * line rate by it), so on the twin 9600 is 95.904 Hz; on a fast 1080p it is the
  * rate itself, with the 1000/1001 flag, and the multiple stays within 120 Hz:
  * more would shorten the time with one eye.
  */
